# [IMPL-PRIME_PRINTER] [ARCH-PRIME_PRINTER] [REQ-PRIME_PRINTER] How: define pure prime detection and ordered collection plus a thin IO printer for the required first-five output.

## IS_PRIME
procedure IS_PRIME(candidate):
  # [IMPL-PRIME_PRINTER] [ARCH-PRIME_PRINTER] [REQ-PRIME_PRINTER] How: classify one candidate with trial division without performing IO.
  Contract:
    INPUT: candidate (integer)
    OUTPUT: boolean
    PRE: candidate is an integer
    POST: result is true exactly when candidate is at least 2 and has no divisor from 2 through the square root of candidate
    EFFECTS: pure
    TERMINATION: total
  # [IMPL-PRIME_PRINTER] [ARCH-PRIME_PRINTER] [REQ-PRIME_PRINTER] How: apply boundary checks and trial division to return the primality result.
  IF candidate < 2: RETURN false
  IF candidate = 2: RETURN true
  FOR divisor IN integers from 2 through floor(square_root(candidate)):
    IF candidate is divisible by divisor: RETURN false
  RETURN true

## COLLECT_FIRST_FIVE_PRIMES
procedure COLLECT_FIRST_FIVE_PRIMES:
  # [IMPL-PRIME_PRINTER] [ARCH-PRIME_PRINTER] [REQ-PRIME_PRINTER] How: build the exact ascending first-five-primes list using only pure operations.
  Contract:
    INPUT: none
    OUTPUT: ordered list of five integers
    PRE: none; the operation has a fixed requested count of five
    POST: result equals [2, 3, 5, 7, 11] and every result is prime
    DATA: primes (list), candidate (integer)
    DATA_TRANSITION: primes starts empty and receives each accepted candidate until size(primes) = 5; candidate increases by one after each inspection
    EFFECTS: pure
    TERMINATION: total — the finite sequence of prime numbers guarantees progress to five accepted candidates
  # [IMPL-PRIME_PRINTER] [ARCH-PRIME_PRINTER] [REQ-PRIME_PRINTER] How: inspect ascending candidates and append only candidates accepted by IS_PRIME until five values exist.
  primes := empty list
  candidate := 2
  WHILE size(primes) < 5:
    IF IS_PRIME(candidate): append candidate to primes
    candidate := candidate + 1
  RETURN primes

## PRINT_FIRST_FIVE_PRIMES
procedure PRINT_FIRST_FIVE_PRIMES(output_stream):
  # [IMPL-PRIME_PRINTER] [ARCH-PRIME_PRINTER] [REQ-PRIME_PRINTER] How: compose pure collection with one-line-per-prime output through an injectable IO stream.
  Contract:
    INPUT: output_stream (IO-like sink; defaults to standard output when omitted)
    OUTPUT: output_stream | error OutputWriteFailed
    PRE: output_stream supports writing a string line
    POST: success appends exactly 2, 3, 5, 7, and 11, each followed by one newline, in that order; error returns OutputWriteFailed
    FAILURE_MODES: OutputWriteFailed
    EFFECTS: IO
    TERMINATION: total — exactly five values are written
  # [IMPL-PRIME_PRINTER] [ARCH-PRIME_PRINTER] [REQ-PRIME_PRINTER] How: collect the pure result, write each prime as one line, and expose write failures without changing the pure modules.
  primes := COLLECT_FIRST_FIVE_PRIMES
  FOR prime IN primes:
    ON error from writing prime followed by newline: RETURN error OutputWriteFailed
  RETURN output_stream